<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hohenstaufen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1079–1268</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Staufer, House of Hohenstaufen, Hohenstaufen dynasty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hohenstaufen, or Staufer, were a Swabian dynasty named after their castle on the Hohenstaufen mountain. Dukes of Swabia from 1079, they became German kings with Conrad III in 1138 and emperors with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a>, Henry VI and Frederick II, who also ruled the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>. Their long conflict with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a> ended in their ruin, and the last of the line, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conradin">Conradin</a>, was executed in 1268.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen.jpg" alt="Hohenstaufen" width="320" height="386" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Ssolbergj · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Or_three_leopards_sable.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
